        "title": "feat: add durable routines registry",
        "body": "Closes #98515\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw has cron jobs, tasks, heartbeat, commitments, and channel/session delivery primitives, but no first-class durable registry for recurring team-operations routines. Operators can schedule work today, but they cannot create, inspect, pause, delete, or recover a typed routine as one durable product object with ownership, delivery target, run status, and replay-safe mutation semantics.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds the smallest complete routine slice: a typed routine registry backed by the shared SQLite state DB, Gateway RPC methods, CLI entrypoints, an agent-tool entrypoint, and a schedule trigger that delegates execution to the canonical cron service rather than creating a second scheduler. The design keeps cron as the scheduler owner and routines as the durable registry owner, with internal create/toggle stages so retries recover safely after partial persistence or scheduler failures.\n\nNon-goals for this draft: no Control UI yet, no channel-watch/repository-event/webhook triggers yet, no duplicate scheduler, and no transcript attachment. The trigger model is shaped so those future triggers can share the same routine subsystem instead of growing a second path.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review were used for this draft PR.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators can now use `openclaw routines`, Gateway RPC, or the Gateway agent tool to create, list, inspect, enable, disable, and delete durable scheduled routines. Routine inspection shows owner, delivery target, enabled/deleted state, last and next run visibility, status, and last error context. Repeated create/toggle/delete calls are idempotent, and restart/replay behavior preserves the intended routine state instead of silently losing a schedule toggle or rolling scheduler state backward.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `786ba1e63a6953c9c12c95fa99abe3b5aaffe7d3`, rebased on `origin/main` `5bcd25f0fb6de3cc2ba6b6a7688a9361eb355143`.\n- LOC gate after final rebase: total 51 files `+6542/-409`; production 27 files `+3103/-390`, tests 11 files `+2805/-0`, docs 9 files `+359/-19`, generated protocol/state files 4 files `+275/-0`. Remaining positive production LOC is concentrated in the routine service durability/recovery state machine, narrow CLI/Gateway/protocol entrypoints, and shared cron validation/scope helpers that delete duplicated cron Gateway policy rather than creating a second scheduler.\n- Exact-head local sanity passed: `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`, `pnpm docs:list`, `pnpm protocol:check`, and clean `git status --porcelain=v1`.\n- Focused local runtime proof passed before the final app/extension-only rebases: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs <routines/cron/Gateway/CLI/protocol/session/tool-result-truncation tests>` completed 5 shards / 156 tests, and targeted `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs <touched runtime/test files>` passed. The later rebases touched only iOS/Android/Discord/Feishu owner files outside the routines/cron/Gateway/protocol lane.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox exact routine scenario passed with provider `blacksmith-testbox`, id `tbx_01kwh57ehx56t754rqjxqttskg`, Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28582551404. The proof matched exact tree `0b6d7d0814271c196c8fae82170f3590c1f12bde`, built the branch, started an isolated local Gateway, approved the staged device scope request, and drove `openclaw routines list/create/list/get/disable/enable/delete` through the public CLI and Gateway RPC. Final assertion output: `{\"routineId\":\"proof-daily\",\"cronJobId\":\"routine-cron-61f944366f18f9191d29a9b0425f6694\",\"backing\":\"linked\",\"status\":\"enabled\",\"deleted\":true,\"persistentTarget\":\"session:agent:ops:main\",\"isolatedTarget\":\"isolated\",\"isolatedDelivery\":\"none\"}`.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox exact changed/build gate passed with provider `blacksmith-testbox`, id `tbx_01kwh5gdg666jm6dm0sknq6taq`, Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28582820315. The proof matched exact tree `0b6d7d0814271c196c8fae82170f3590c1f12bde`, then ran `corepack pnpm build:strict-smoke` and `corepack pnpm check:changed` with remote changed lanes enabled.\n- Fresh autoreview against `origin/main` passed clean on exact head with model `koffing-updated`, extra-high reasoning: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main --engine codex --model codex=koffing-updated --thinking codex=xhigh --prompt-file <prompt-file> --output <review-output> --json-output <review-json>`. It explicitly reassessed best-fix fit, owner boundaries, LOC pressure, cron helper duplication, idempotent mutations, drift handling, re-enable behavior, docs/generated alignment, and PR evidence hygiene; result: no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nRisks and review focus: routine persistence and cron mutation ordering, idempotent replay after partial failures, schema/client drift, schedule-only routine views over mutable cron backing jobs, and delivery target defaults. No UI screenshot evidence is included because this draft intentionally defers Control UI work.\n",
